  "version": 1,
  "comments": {
    "c1": {
      "anchor": "mapping#markdown-5",
      "kind": "markdown",
      "label": "4. How it maps to the protocol",
      "excerpt": "It's still a real ATSpace, but with a single writer. The authority's own account",
      "text": "So this means that some things are written by the author, and some by spell.  Could we generalize this, so that content I write always goes in my repo, and we just link to it from the \"org repos\"?",
      "by": "owenoak",
      "at": "2026-11-02T01:55:11.582Z",
      "status": "answered",
      "quote": "Posts and comments are",
      "offset": 313,
      "edited": "2026-11-02T01:56:12.249Z",
      "replies": [
        {
          "by": "owenoak",
          "agent": "claude",
          "at": "2026-11-02T01:57:07.146Z",
          "html": "<p>Yes, mostly, and it's a cleaner rule:  <b>what a person writes is theirs, and what the org decides is the org's.</b>  The org's record becomes a link saying \"this version of Ana's page is the group's page\".  I haven't changed the doc yet, as there's a choice to make.</p>\n<p><b>What gets better:</b></p>\n<ul>\n  <li>The doc no longer sets aside the protocol's \"authority rests with the author\".</li>\n  <li>Other apps see the real author, and the history shows who wrote each version.</li>\n  <li>Spell still has the final say, by refusing to link.  A Lead \"deletes\" by removing the link.</li>\n  <li>If the write server is down, people can still write;  it links when it's back.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><b>What doesn't move:</b>  sign-ups, sheet rows, roles and the links themselves stay the org's.  They're decisions, so the last ticket and \"Ana edits Bo's row\" still work.</p>\n<p><b>The three costs:</b></p>\n<ol>\n  <li><b>Private spaces:</b>  if Ana has an account on her own host, she keeps the budget notes after she leaves, and the org can't remove them.  This is the serious one.</li>\n  <li><b>Pages can break:</b>  if Ana deletes her page, or her host is down, the group's page is gone, unless the org keeps a copy of what it links to.</li>\n  <li><b>Slower reads:</b>  one page can mean fetching from several hosts.</li>\n</ol>\n<p><b>My recommendation:</b>  use it in public spaces, with the org keeping a copy of each linked page and file, and leave private spaces the org's.  None of this has been tested against the protocol yet.</p>"
        },
        {
          "by": "owenoak",
          "at": "2026-11-02T01:57:58.269Z",
          "text": "So comments and posts, no problem.\nFor pages, what if everything in Ana's account is a draft, and it only goes into the public repo on \"publish\"?\nCould we then delete it from Ana's account -- assuming that her account didn't come from her own host?",
          "edited": "2026-11-02T01:59:16.586Z"
        }
      ],
      "claim": {
        "by": "owenoak",
